    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, reading the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and every function it invokes. The entire pipeline runs under one `transaction` governance, so all DB writes commit once at the very end (or roll back on any escalation).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **[Validation] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `CheckIdempotency`\n- **[Side-effect] Publish `Idempotency-Key`** header value (may be null) as a variable for later recording.\n- **[Validation/short-circuit] Idempotency replay** \u2014 if the key is present and already recorded in `IdempotencyStore`, it loads the originally-created owner and throws `IdempotentReplayException`, short-circuiting to **200 OK** with that owner. No new owner is created (it deliberately returns before the 409 duplicate check).\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `BuildOwner` (binds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`)\nBean-validation on the DTO runs first (`@Valid`), producing `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** on failure:\n- **[Validation] firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`.\n- **[Validation] lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`.\n- **[Validation] address** \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; **addressLine1/addressLine2** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`.\n- **[Validation] city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n- **[Validation] telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`.\n- **[Validation] email** \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`.\n- **[Validation] postcode** \u2014 pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`.\n\nThen in the method body, in this order:\n- **[Side-effect] Publish `sharesHousehold`** flag (`true`/`false`) as a variable.\n- **[Side-effect] Normalize address fields** \u2014 `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE), blank\u2192null; then compose the effective `address`, preferring the structured lines over the flat `address`.\n- **[Validation] Required fields present** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank (after composition), else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **[Side-effect + Validation] Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 strip separators; keep `+`/country code or assume `+61` (dropping one leading `0`); must be `+` then 8\u201315 digits, and for `+61` exactly 9 / for `+1` exactly 10 national digits, else `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**. Stored normalized.\n- **[Side-effect + Validation] Email normalize** (optional) \u2014 blank/null left as-is; otherwise must be syntactically valid and not a disposable domain (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com), else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**. Stored lower-cased.\n- **[Validation] Postcode** (optional) \u2014 if the city has a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) the postcode must fall in range, else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode.\n- **[Side-effect] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity.**\n- **[Validation] Registration date not in future** \u2014 if a date is supplied and is after today, `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **[Side-effect] Set registration date** \u2014 supplied date, or today if none; then roll forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday list). Downstream day-based logic uses this adjusted date.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `AssignHousehold`\n- **[Side-effect] Set `householdId`** = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Assigned unconditionally.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- **[Validation] Household uniqueness** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, reject with `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409** if any existing non-soft-deleted owner resolves to the same `householdId`.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **[Side-effect] Set `customerCode`** = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode range, else city table, else `UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of `SHA-256(telephone + lastName)`), appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 on collision with an existing owner's code.\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **[Side-effect] Set `namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners with the same first + last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **[Validation] City capacity** \u2014 reject with `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409** if the owner's city already has \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed).\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`\n- **[Validation] Daily limit** \u2014 reject with `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429** if \u2265 100 existing owners share this owner's (adjusted) registration date.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- **[Side-effect] Set `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 declared household members are left `false`; otherwise flag `true` with the lowest-id matching owner when a non-soft-deleted owner shares the `householdId` but has a different telephone (else `false`).\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **[Side-effect] Persist the owner** via `OwnerRepository.save` (id assigned).\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `RecordIdempotency`\n- **[Side-effect] Record idempotency** \u2014 if the request carried a key, store `key \u2192 owner.id` so a later repeat replays this owner. No-op when no key.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **[Side-effect] Emit AUDIT log line** \u2014 id, customerCode, registrationDate, and the derived membershipPoints/membershipLevel/membershipNumber (computed here for logging only, not persisted).\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **[Side-effect] Respond 201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body. The single transaction commits at pipeline end.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the \"validations\" in steps 4, 7, 8 and the duplicate/namesake/customer-code logic all call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and scan in memory (not indexed queries), and the uniqueness/capacity/limit checks are read-then-write within one transaction, so they are subject to races between concurrent creates. Let me know if you'd like me to look into either."
